---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import {
  PROVEN,
  NOT_PROVEN,
  DETERMINISM_STATEMENT,
  ENTROPY_STATEMENT,
  HOMEPAGE_STATUS,
  HISTORICAL_PROTOTYPE_SCOPE,
} from '../data/bytelite';
import { COMPANY_NAME, FOUNDER_NAME, COMPANY_LOCATION } from '../data/company';
import { FOUNDER_CARDS, cardIsActionable } from '../data/commerce';

// Company-voice rebuild, 2026-08-31.
//
// The long technical dossier that used to live here moved to /how-it-works and /validation. This
// page has one job: say what ByteLite is, what ByteLite LLC has actually established, what is
// still open, and where to go next.
//
// VOICE: this is the company speaking. "I", "me" and "my" appear in exactly one place on this
// site - the signed founder note below - and nowhere else on any page. The rule exists because
// founder-singular commercial copy reads as a personal undertaking, and licensing, billing and
// support obligations belong to ByteLite LLC.
//
// The status strip is derived from ROADMAP in src/data/bytelite.ts, never typed here, so a gate
// cannot look further along on the homepage than it is in the canonical record.
const cards = FOUNDER_CARDS.map((c) => ({ ...c, actionable: cardIsActionable(c) }));
---

<Layout
  title="ByteLite | Every file builds its own route."
  description="ByteLite is deterministic recursive compression built from the structure of the file itself. The original returns exactly, or the result does not count."
  keywords="ByteLite, deterministic compression, exact reconstruction, lossless, ByteLite LLC"
  canonical="https://www.thebytelite.com/"
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">{COMPANY_NAME}</p>
      <h1 class="hero-h1">Every file builds its own route.</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">
        ByteLite is deterministic recursive compression built from the structure of the file
        itself. The original returns exactly, or the result does not count.
      </p>
      <p class="rule-strip">Exact reconstruction. Complete representation. Deterministic operation.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a href="/how-it-works" class="btn btn-primary">See How ByteLite Works</a>
        <a href="/validation" class="btn btn-outline">Review the Evidence</a>
        <a href="/founder-access" class="btn btn-ghost">Founder Access</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHERE THE WORK STANDS.
       One status section, deliberately. The previous build repeated a warning on every section of
       every page, which buried the technology under its own disclaimer. Qualification lives here
       and, in full, on /validation. -->
  <section class="section-sm">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="status-h">Where the work stands.</h2>
      <ul class="status">
        {HOMEPAGE_STATUS.map((s) => (
          <li>
            <span class="status-l">{s.label}</span>
            <span class="status-n">{s.note}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      {/* The scope line sits with the list, not in a footnote. The prototype result is a real
          company-reported demonstration; the two things a reader could wrongly take from it are
          that today's encoder does it automatically and that somebody outside checked it. */}
      <p class="status-scope">{HISTORICAL_PROTOTYPE_SCOPE}</p>
      <p class="after"><a href="/validation">Every claim, with the evidence behind it &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Brand hero graphic. Eager + high priority: it is the largest element on the first screen,
       so lazy-loading it would delay the LCP rather than help it. -->
  <section class="section-sm">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <img
        class="fig"
        src="/bytelite/bytelite-stack-hero.webp"
        alt="ByteLite: deterministic compression, evidence before claims. Built for individuals, organizations and technical review."
        width="1400" height="788"
        loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHY -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Why this exists.</h2>
      <p class="body">
        Storing and moving data costs real money, and most of what gets stored is described far less
        efficiently than it could be. That part is not controversial. What is hard is doing better
        without ever guessing &mdash; because the moment a system guesses, it is no longer returning
        your file, it is returning something that resembles it.
      </p>
      <p class="body">
        ByteLite is the honest version of that. It reads structure from the file itself and builds
        its reduction route from what it finds, rather than forcing every input through one fixed
        statistical model. {DETERMINISM_STATEMENT}
      </p>
      <p class="body">{ENTROPY_STATEMENT}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THREE RULES -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Three rules ByteLite LLC will not trade away.</h2>
      <ol class="rules">
        <li>
          <h3>Exact reconstruction</h3>
          <p>The bytes that come out match the bytes that went in, or the attempt failed. There is
          no "close enough" and no partial credit.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Complete counting</h3>
          <p>Any size claim is measured from the complete artifact. Moving part of the cost
          somewhere uncounted is not compression, it is bookkeeping.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Deterministic operation</h3>
          <p>Same input, same result, every time. No confidence scores, no sampling, nothing that
          needs a retry to land on the right answer.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- EVIDENCE -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>What is actually proven.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Claims move up only when the evidence behind them moves up. Here is where each one sits
        today.
      </p>

      <img
        class="fig"
        src="/bytelite/proof-before-claim-ladder.webp"
        alt="Proof-before-claim progression from concept through prototype, proof artifact, validation, and product."
        width="1400" height="788" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
      />

      <div class="two-col">
        <div>
          <h3 class="col-h col-yes">Proven internally</h3>
          <ul class="list list-yes">{PROVEN.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="col-h col-no">Not proven</h3>
          <ul class="list list-no">{NOT_PROVEN.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="after"><a href="/validation">The full evidence, category by category &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT IT COULD CHANGE -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>What it would change, if it works.</h2>
      <p class="body">
        Smaller representations mean less to store and less to move. That is the entire commercial
        idea, and it is why the licensing model only charges against savings somebody actually
        measured.
      </p>
      <p class="body">
        There is no percentage on this page. ByteLite LLC does not have a verified one, and a
        number nobody measured is exactly what this site exists to avoid. When there is a real
        figure, it will arrive with the measurement attached.
      </p>
      <p class="after"><a href="/licensing">How pricing and licensing would work &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHERE TO START -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Where to start.</h2>
      <img
        class="fig"
        src="/bytelite/audience-entry-cards.webp"
        alt="Starting points for people, organizations, and technical reviewers."
        width="1400" height="788" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
      />
      <!-- Real links, not a clickable image. The graphic above is decoration for these three. -->
      <div class="paths">
        <a class="path" href="/founder-access">
          <span class="path-t">For people</span>
          <span class="path-d">Founder access to ByteLite, Cordel Connect and Cordel Play.</span>
        </a>
        <a class="path" href="/licensing">
          <span class="path-t">For organizations</span>
          <span class="path-d">Licensing, integration and the savings-share model.</span>
        </a>
        <a class="path" href="/validation">
          <span class="path-t">For technical reviewers</span>
          <span class="path-d">Evidence, current status and the known limitations.</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FOUNDER ACCESS -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Founder access.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        None of these products is available yet, so none of them charges you. Each card says the
        state it is really in.
      </p>
      <ul class="fa-list">
        {cards.map((card) => (
          <li>
            <a href={card.href}>{card.title}</a>
            <span class={card.actionable ? 'fa-tag fa-open' : 'fa-tag fa-shut'}>
              {card.actionable ? 'Reservation open' : 'Being configured'}
            </span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="after"><a href="/founder-access">Founder access &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE COMPANY -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Who builds it.</h2>
      <p class="body">
        {COMPANY_NAME} is a founder-led technology company in {COMPANY_LOCATION}. It is small on
        purpose: there is no marketing function positioned to turn an unfinished result into a
        finished claim, and every statement on this site is answerable to the evidence behind it.
      </p>
      <p class="after"><a href="/about">About {COMPANY_NAME} &rarr;</a></p>

      {/* THE ONE FOUNDER NOTE.
          First-person singular is confined to this block and does not appear anywhere else on the
          public site. It is labelled and signed so a reader can tell a personal statement from
          company copy - which is the whole reason the rest of the site stopped using "I". */}
      <blockquote class="founder">
        <p class="founder-label">A note from {FOUNDER_NAME}</p>
        <p>
          I started this because the honest version of the problem was more interesting than the
          marketable one. I am responsible for what this site says, and I can be asked about any of
          it directly.
        </p>
        <p>If a result fails, it stays failed until the code proves otherwise.</p>
        <footer class="founder-sign">{FOUNDER_NAME}, founder, {COMPANY_NAME}</footer>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CONTACT -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <img
        class="fig"
        src="/bytelite/contact-cta-banner.webp"
        alt="ByteLite LLC contact invitation for general inquiries, licensing and technical review."
        width="1400" height="788" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
      />
      <h2 class="cta-h">Talk with {COMPANY_NAME}.</h2>
      <p class="body">
        General inquiries, licensing, technical review, founder access and product questions are
        all welcome, and they reach the company directly. Evidence that falsifies something on this
        site is the most useful message it can receive.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Contact {COMPANY_NAME}</a>
        <a href="/validation" class="btn btn-outline">Read the evidence first</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>

<style>
.narrow { max-width: 820px; }

.hero { padding: 5.5rem 0 3rem; background: radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 60% at 50% -10%, rgba(99,102,241,.1) 0%, transparent 70%); }
.hero-inner { max-width: 820px; }
.hero-h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3.5rem); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
.hero-sub { max-width: 660px; font-size: 1.0625rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.75; }
.rule-strip {
  margin-top: 1.75rem; padding: .875rem 1.125rem; max-width: 660px;
  font-size: .9375rem; font-weight: 600; color: #c4c8f0;
  background: rgba(99,102,241,.07); border-left: 3px solid #6366f1; border-radius: .5rem;
}
.hero-cta { display: flex; gap: .875rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 2rem; }
@media (max-width: 540px) { .hero { padding: 3.5rem 0 2rem; } }

/* Every graphic: intrinsic width/height on the tag reserves the 16:9 box, height:auto keeps the
   ratio, so nothing shifts and nothing stretches. */
.fig {
  display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 0 0 2rem;
  border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-radius: .75rem; background: #0d1120;
}

h2 { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
h3 { font-size: 1rem; color: #e4e7f2; margin-bottom: .5rem; }
.lede { font-size: 1.0625rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1.75rem; max-width: 660px; }
.body { font-size: 1rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.8; margin-top: 1rem; max-width: 660px; }
.after { margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: .9375rem; }
.after a { color: #818cf8; font-weight: 500; }
.after a:hover, .after a:focus-visible { color: #a5b4fc; }

.rules { list-style: none; counter-reset: r; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
.rules li {
  counter-increment: r; position: relative;
  padding: 1.125rem 1.25rem 1.125rem 3.25rem;
  background: #0d1120; border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-radius: .625rem;
}
.rules li::before {
  content: counter(r); position: absolute; left: 1.125rem; top: 1.125rem;
  width: 1.5rem; height: 1.5rem; border-radius: 50%;
  background: rgba(99,102,241,.15); color: #a5b4fc;
  display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: .8125rem; font-weight: 700;
}
.rules p { font-size: .9375rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0; }

.two-col { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; }
@media (max-width: 640px) { .two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
.col-h { font-size: .6875rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
.col-yes { color: #34d399; }
.col-no { color: #f472b6; }
.list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: .5rem; }
.list li {
  font-size: .875rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.6;
  padding: .625rem .875rem; background: #0d1120;
  border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-left: 3px solid #34d399; border-radius: .5rem;
}
.list-no li { border-left-color: #f472b6; }

.paths { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
.path {
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .375rem;
  padding: 1.125rem; background: #0d1120;
  border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-radius: .625rem;
  text-decoration: none; transition: border-color .15s;
}
.path:hover, .path:focus-visible { border-color: #6366f1; }
.path-t { font-size: .9375rem; font-weight: 600; color: #e4e7f2; }
.path-d { font-size: .8125rem; color: #7b829e; line-height: 1.55; }

.fa-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: .5rem; }
.fa-list li {
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
  padding: .75rem .875rem; background: #0d1120;
  border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-radius: .5rem;
}
.fa-list a { font-size: .9375rem; color: #e4e7f2; }
.fa-tag { font-size: .6875rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
.fa-open { color: #34d399; }
.fa-shut { color: #7b829e; }

/* One status block for the whole page. Label and note are separate elements so the state and its
   qualifier are never collapsed into a single sentence that can be quoted without the caveat. */
.status-h { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
.status { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: .5rem; }
.status li {
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .25rem;
  padding: .875rem 1rem; background: #0d1120;
  border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-left: 3px solid #6366f1; border-radius: .5rem;
}
.status-l { font-size: .9375rem; font-weight: 600; color: #e4e7f2; line-height: 1.5; }
.status-n { font-size: .8438rem; color: #7b829e; line-height: 1.6; }
.status-scope {
  margin-top: 1rem; max-width: 660px;
  font-size: .875rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.7;
  padding-left: .875rem; border-left: 2px solid #2a3350;
}

.founder {
  margin: 2rem 0 0; padding: 1.75rem;
  background: #0d1120; border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-left: 3px solid #818cf8;
  border-radius: .75rem;
}
.founder p { font-size: 1rem; color: #c4c8f0; line-height: 1.8; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
.founder-label {
  font-size: .6875rem !important; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em;
  text-transform: uppercase; color: #818cf8 !important; margin-bottom: .875rem !important;
}
.founder-sign { font-size: .8125rem; color: #7b829e; font-style: normal; }
.cta-h { margin-top: 0; }
</style>
